https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/valentines-day-what-is-the-point.png?fit=685%2C685&amp;ssl=1\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-label=\"Open image 2 of 2 in full-screen\"srcset=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/valentines-day-what-is-the-point.png?strip=info&#038;w=600 600w,https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/valentines-day-what-is-the-point.png?strip=info&#038;w=800 800w\" alt=\"\" data-height=\"800\" data-id=\"806\" data-link=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/valentines-day-what-is-the-point\/\" data-url=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/valentines-day-what-is-the-point.png\" data-width=\"800\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/valentines-day-what-is-the-point.png?w=685&#038;ssl=1\" data-amp-layout=\"responsive\" \/><\/figure><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">But the &#8216;sketch&#8217; I used to work out how to draw the polygon bar charts probably makes no sense to anyone but me. And even I don&#8217;t understand what I did now!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"484\" height=\"290\" data-attachment-id=\"984\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/mm_21_7_sketch2\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/mm_21_7_sketch2.png?fit=484%2C290&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"484,290\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"mm_21_7_sketch2\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/mm_21_7_sketch2.png?fit=484%2C290&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/04\/mm_21_7_sketch2.png?resize=484%2C290&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-984\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-light-gray-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Summary<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A few things I have noted while going through this:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><li>I am either a) very good at getting an initial design so don&#8217;t need to deviate or b) am just stubborn and won&#8217;t change it even if I need to! Most likely b).<\/li><li>Sketching can help by stop me from building something I don&#8217;t like\/wont work. A few of the sketches I have pivoted on at some point and ended up building something different.<\/li><li>I shouldn&#8217;t be afraid to do multiple differing sketches. As in note 1, I don&#8217;t often do multiple sketches, but when I have I feel I have explored the subject more thoroughly.<\/li><li>Comparing sketch vs. final is fun! Even if it has gone in a completely different direction!<\/li><\/ol>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">All the rest of the comparisons can be found here: <a href=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/sketches-vs-reality\/\">Sketches vs Reality<\/a> and I will keep this up to date as I do more sketches.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Hope you found this interesting!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Ant.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Some comparisons of previous sketches I have done vs. the final design in Tableau.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":191258845,"featured_media":1036,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_coblocks_attr":"","_coblocks_dimension